cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Enterprise Knowledge Ontology (EKO) and the Corpus Readiness Index"
message: "If you use this ontology, the publish gate or the Corpus Readiness Index, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Fabio
    family-names: Rovai
    affiliation: "Kampakis and Co Ltd (The Tesseract Academy)"
    email: fabio@thetesseractacademy.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/fabio-rovai/enterprise-knowledge-ontology"
abstract: >-
  An OWL vocabulary formalising the distinction between working documents and
  authoritative knowledge assets via the notion of a maintenance commitment, a
  SHACL publish gate enforcing it, and a seven-dimension measurement instrument
  for organisational knowledge corpora, validated against 54,222 documents of
  the GOV.UK guidance estate.
keywords:
  - ontology
  - SHACL
  - knowledge management
  - knowledge architecture
  - corpus readiness
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - information governance
  - records management
  - register assurance
